on's fundraising advantage and a favorable national environment have largely erased Marshall's incumbency edge in an R+8 state; polls give Hamilton about a one-point edge while markets and eight of eleven raters call it a Tossup, leaving the race effectively even.", "watch": "Whether Marshall consolidates Republican-leaning voters in the closing days, as markets and Kansas's baseline suggest, or Hamilton's polling edge and financial advantage hold through Election Day.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Roger Marshall (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kansas has rarely hosted a competitive Senate race, but this one sits on a knife's edge. Senator Roger Marshall seeks a second term against Adam Hamilton, a well-known moderate Methodist pastor who has outraised the incumbent roughly three to one and kept the contest tied on the airwaves. A Democratic-leaning national environment has largely neutralized the state's eight-point Republican tilt and the usual incumbent advantage.\n\nPolling across the fall shows a dead heat: thirteen surveys average to roughly a one-point Democratic edge, with the latest high-quality poll giving Hamilton a four-point lead. Prediction markets and several raters still lean narrowly toward Marshall, and eight of eleven ratings call the race a Tossup. With the fundamentals favoring the incumbent and the polls favoring the challenger, the race enters Election Day as a genuine coin flip.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2893, "margin": -2.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3585, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4222, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4301, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3024, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2988, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4183, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4225, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3457, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_de